--
[temp.deduct]/5: deduced template parameter values are available to subsequent
default template arguments.  A constructor template constrained by a SFINAE
default argument whose constexpr callee (a member of another class template)
uses the constructor's own deduced parameter pack now resolves: the deduced
pack ELEMENT TYPES are recorded before default template arguments are
evaluated, so the constraint folds over the real arguments instead of an empty
list.  The shape of std::tuple's constrained constructors under
std::make_tuple.  Cross-checked against g++ and clang++.
